  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA multiprofile with scvi_n200 and transformer aggregation is much better than single-profile RNA models, especially compared with scvi_n200 single-profile and pca_n2000 single-profile. The key uncertainty is whether this gain comes from the multiprofile/transformer design generally or specifically from the scvi_n200 representation. config_003 keeps model setting, profile setting, and aggregation fixed while changing only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to pca_n2000, directly isolating the representation effect. This is a high-value one-factor experiment before spending budget on more complex multimodal fusion choices."
}

